vements leaving many of them feeling  stuck and of course fearing deportation  nate  now we normally don't see haitian  migrants in large numbers at the  southern border why is this happening  now  well many of them fled the island nation  after that devastating earthquake in  2010 and obtained jobs in south america  including in the run-up and during the  olympics in brazil but largely due to  the pandemic those jobs have dried up  and rumors spread that this was the best  place to try to enter the u.s  manuel bajorcas in del rio texas thank  you
 

